# runpod — vLLM on a rented GPU pod, reached over HTTPS.
#
# The backend is `remote_openai`, NOT `vllm`. RunPod's vllm template runs the
# engine itself, so there is no local process for us to own: `vllm.py` spawns
# and supervises, here we only proxy. RunPod is a deployment of remote_openai,
# not a fourth backend (ADR-0007, docs/BACKENDS.md §2.3).
#
# Two values cannot live here. The pod id changes every deployment, and the
# upstream key is a secret — set both in .env.local, or export them:
#
#     RUNPOD_POD_ID=<pod id>              # or HARNESS_REMOTE_BASE_URL=https://...
#     HARNESS_REMOTE_API_KEY=<the pod's --api-key>
#
# The catalog below is *generated* by scripts/profiles/runpod.sh from what the
# pod reports at /v1/models. It is not committed: it describes one pod serving
# one model, and both change every time you start a pod.
#
# Known limitation: one pod serves one model, so switching between catalog
# entries is instant and does nothing.

HARNESS_DEFAULT_BACKEND=remote_openai
HARNESS_MODELS_FILE=.local/models.runpod.yaml
HARNESS_STATE_DIR=.local
RUNPOD_POD_PORT=8000
